{"title":"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two candles of the same height are lighted at the same time. The first is consumed in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours and the second in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours. \nAssuming that each candle burns at a constant rate, in how many hours after being lighted was the first candle twice the height of the second? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eeb487f1076ca02bad67e5a93426d24e43fb1789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1\\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2\\frac{2}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"391\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> hours, the height of the first candle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d149220df10933f1eb2fe8558d48d965bbea7b95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\frac{x}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"34\" /> and the height of the second candle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6b63cf736d952029717bca7b84cee6235eea53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\frac{x}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"34\" /> Essentially, we are solving the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/342d77e749b9eb2b91c7acba37be61be0f344880.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 - \\frac{x}{4} = 2(1 - \\frac{x}{3})\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04aab39cacc33a44768cf86f345da85d7b6bd4a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- \\frac{x}{4} = 1 - \\frac{2x}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"38\" /> | <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1cdce6acda51a9f91f1ee346973c354d5ec7ec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- 3x = 12 - 8x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"15\" /> | <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/21125614f2841b11b5376a032007a3b00d9333fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdot 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a5c0a452e7986e0c22e79f9c36d9d7350c1e8ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> | <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8cdac3d3c30f0f0ea733083966a15d26c230345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+8x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bfefdf055d92981ad20084cb38534853e11bc69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{12}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" /> | <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28d63667c79306e2a1cf363fcfbc5024205fddd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6a6c853b27182f1be29493f306d101235896a52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\quad 2 \\frac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"116\" height=\"49\" /> hours.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME\" title=\"1956 AHSME\">1956 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1956 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1956\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>